A||||6||watts||Cradle holder||||3||
Z||000000||watts||12-11-2001||01:23 AM||||I think someone had been asking about a cradle holder/mover.  Well, I finally got around to making mine.  Picture says a thousand words, so here's some...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cradle_stand_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cradle_stand_2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cradle_stand_3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cradle_stand_4.jpg"> <P>The dimensions, if anyone wants to build there own....<P>28" front to back<BR>34" side to side<BR>6" high pillars<BR>28.5" center to center on the locating/holding pins (seen in #3)<BR>I used fixed 3" casters in the front, and 3" swivel casters in the rear.<P>Note: this fits my '88 cradle quite nicely - I don't know if the earlier ones are exactly the same.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Standard||12-11-2001||02:14 AM||||bingo!  That's exactly what I've been looking for!  thank you!<P>Now to try and clean out the garage.. and find the time and money to drop the engine and replace what i want to..<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-11-2001||06:54 AM||||I went to Home Depot and bought a dolly for $25 or so - works fine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||revin||12-11-2001||07:17 AM||||Looks great! So can that be used to remove the cradle? I mean jack the car up so far, take off some stuff and attach the cradle to the stand, finish jacking the car for clearance then sliding the engine and cradle out all as one?||||reg||1
Z||000004||watts||12-11-2001||12:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by revin:<BR><B>Looks great! So can that be used to remove the cradle? I mean jack the car up so far, take off some stuff and attach the cradle to the stand, finish jacking the car for clearance then sliding the engine and cradle out all as one?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That was the plan - I'll see how well it works in action.  I made it really low so it'd tuck under the car easily.  The stand offs are there for exhaust clearance.  Mounting bolts are still all visible.<P>Cost? <BR>Lumber $20<BR>Lag bolts $5<BR>Casters $40<BR>All in Canadian funds - so about $3us.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Banzai||12-11-2001||04:47 PM||||I was going to make something like that but when I borrowed my neigbors engine stand(two piece, higher capacity) I found that the bottom U shaped piece with caster on it was the perfect size. Then I just borrowed another engine stand. Worked out great.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||88-DOHC||12-11-2001||05:13 PM||||Man, with those standoffs hope you like jacking your car WAY up in the air.  From my experience your dolly would probably be just fine without the 6" standoffs. Otherwise, you will probably end up having to jack the front up just so you don't plant your fascia into the floor.<P>||||reg||1
